## 6. PostgreSQL Database Design

Design a normalized relational schema using Prisma.

Include appropriate models for:
- User
- Category
- Product
- Cart
- CartItem
- Order
- OrderItem
- InventoryMovement
- StoreSetting, or an equivalent settings model

Use enums where appropriate for role, order status, and payment status.

Relationships must use appropriate primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, indexes, and deletion policies.

Requirements:
- Unique user email
- Unique product SKU
- Unique product slug
- Unique category slug
- Unique order number
- A single active cart per authenticated customer
- A unique product entry per cart
- Valid product and category relationships
- Appropriate createdAt and updatedAt fields
- Historical order items preserved even when a product changes
- Correct decimal monetary storage and calculations
- Database transactions for checkout and stock adjustments

Use PostgreSQL Decimal or another appropriate precise monetary representation. Never use floating-point arithmetic as the authoritative method for calculating money.

Use database constraints and transactional business logic instead of relying only on frontend validation.

Generate and apply Prisma migrations using documented, supported commands. Do not use destructive database resets on an existing database.

